# renovate.json sets no dependency policy of its own — it only maps dependency
# types onto commit prefixes so release-please can section them. Everything
# that governs what gets updated, and when, comes from
# github>krypsis-io/renovate-config, which sets "minimumReleaseAge": "3 days"
# at the top level and fast-tracks vulnerability updates past it.
#
# Semgrep cannot resolve `extends`, so renovate-missing-minimum-release-age
# fires on every packageRules entry here regardless. Setting the key locally is
# worse than leaving it off: these rules match vulnerability updates too, and
# later rules win, so a local value would silently re-impose the delay on
# security patches that the preset deliberately exempts.
#
# 3 days is the accepted org policy. Revisit if this file ever grows a rule
# that actually changes update timing.
renovate.json
